# Testing

- Choose the appropriate layer according to `docs/testing-strategy.md`.
- Test observable behavior, business rules, and boundary contracts.
- Use accessible queries and interactions that closely match real user actions.
- Cover success, loading, error, retry, empty, and relevant edge cases.
- Avoid large snapshots and assertions about library internals.
- Mock Highcharts only at the component boundary; test options and synchronization separately.
- Use the real `json-server` in successful e2e scenarios and `cy.intercept` for controlled failures.
- Do not depend on exact request counts when React StrictMode may duplicate effects in development.
- Keep test data deterministic without unnecessarily duplicating the official dataset.
- Every fixed bug MUST receive a regression test when it can be reproduced reliably.
